From: local fix for HEIC HDR gainmap JPEG forwarding
Subject: [TEMP] jpegsave: forward to uhdrsave when "gainmap" image is present

Source: local (complements upstream PR libvips/libvips#5132 heifload part).
Applies to: vips v8.18.7 (verified: patch -p1 --dry-run clean).
Purpose: jpegsave currently forwards to uhdrsave only on "gainmap-data" or
scRGB. HEIC heifload (patched) attaches only "gainmap" (VImage, no
"gainmap-data"), so Samsung/Apple HEIC thumbs fall through to plain JPEG
(SDR, no MPF). Also check "gainmap" so they encode as UltraHDR.
TODO: Remove this patch + its block in build-camera-extras.sh once upstream
libvips forwards jpegsave to uhdrsave on "gainmap" (or heifload provides
"gainmap-data").
---
--- a/libvips/foreign/jpegsave.c
+++ b/libvips/foreign/jpegsave.c
@@ -156,6 +156,7 @@
 
 	if (have_uhdr &&
 		(vips_image_get_typeof(save->ready, "gainmap-data") ||
+		 vips_image_get_typeof(save->ready, "gainmap") ||
 		 save->ready->Type == VIPS_INTERPRETATION_scRGB)) {
 		/* Pass on to uhdrsave.
 		 */
